    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Paleoceanography",
    "problem": "The exact nature of ocean circulation during the Last Glacial Maximum and its contribution to lower atmospheric CO\u2082 levels remain poorly constrained and debated, hindering a complete understanding of past climate dynamics.",
    "method": "The proposed method uses a global compilation of radiocarbon ventilation age estimates to constrain glacial deep-ocean circulation and carbon residence time, and then applies a carbon partitioning framework to quantify the impact of these changes on atmospheric CO2.",
    "task": "The task is to use a global dataset of radiocarbon measurements to constrain ocean circulation during the Last Glacial Maximum and quantify its impact on the storage of carbon in the deep ocean and the corresponding reduction in atmospheric CO2.",
